<title>SWITZERLAND: WTO sets panel in Mexico-Guatemala cement row.</title>
<headline>WTO sets panel in Mexico-Guatemala cement row.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Trade Organisation on Thursday agreed to a Mexican request for a panel to look into measures by Guatemala against cement imports.</p>
<p>Mexico argues that an anti-dumping investigation launched by the Guatemalan authorities violates a WTO agreement which aims to regulate such actions.</p>
<p>It also complains that during the Guatemalan investigation actions had been taken which also ran against the WTO's underlying accord, the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade.</p>
<p>The United States and Canada, who also export cement to Guatemala, indicated support for the Mexican complaint.</p>
<p>Geneva Newsroom -- 41 22 751 09 91</p>
</text>
